{"type":"message","id":"dba8164a","parentId":"b50b148d","timestamp":"2026-02-21T23:01:50.790Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The script executed successfully and returned a nicely formatted report of Notion tasks from yesterday 07:00 to today 07:00 KST. The report is in Korean, which makes sense given the timezone is Asia/Seoul.\n\nNow I need to present this to Sam in my normal assistant voice (Antigravity 🌌) as plain text. The output is already well-formatted, so I'll just present it clearly.\n\nSince this is a cron job that explicitly says \"Present the results clearly to Sam in your normal assistant voice\", I should deliver this as plain text output (which will be delivered automatically according to the instructions).\n\nThe script output is comprehensive - it shows 12 items with different categories (action_required, fyi, question), senders, and summaries. I'll present this in a friendly, clear manner.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Good morning, Sam! 🌌\n\nHere's your daily Notion briefing for the past 24 hours (02/21 07:00 ~ 02/22 07:00 KST):\n\n---\n\n📅 **Yesterday's Activity Overview**\n\nYou had **12 items** tracked in Notion during this period. Here's what's on your radar:\n\n---\n\n## 🔥 Action Required (5 items)\n\n**1. Azure VM Boot Error - Weekend Support Option**\n- **From:** Justin Gross (Microsoft)\n- **The Situation:** Your Azure VM boot error case was reassigned to APAC engineers after you requested timezone adjustment. Since it's a Sev B case, it won't be processed over the weekend unless you bump the severity.\n- **Action:** Decide if you need immediate weekend support - if so, increase case severity.\n\n**2. NAT VM Patching Notification**\n- **From:** Daniel Gujjarlapudi (AB InBev Security)\n- **The Situation:** Patching is starting now on the MGMTNATPAKRP NAT VM. Daniel wants to know ASAP if you have any concerns.\n- **Action:** Notify them if you have issues with the patching. Make sure to include cloud-security@ab-inbev.com in all replies.\n\n**3. Azure VM Recovery Decision Needed**\n- **From:** Justin Gross (Microsoft)\n- **The Situation:** Microsoft recommends trying offline OS repair first for the boot error (since this VM hosts Oracle DB, it minimizes database consistency risks). If you prefer restore from backup, they strongly recommend involving the Oracle DBA to validate database consistency afterward.\n- **Action:** Choose your recovery path (offline OS repair OR restore + DBA validation) and inform Justin.\n\n**4. Recovery Path Confirmation**\n- **From:** Justin Gross (Microsoft)\n- **The Situation:** Same as above - Justin needs to know which recovery option you want to proceed with so they can start the support process.\n- **Action:** Reply to Justin with your decision.\n\n**5. DBA Involvement for Restore Option**\n- **From:** Justin Gross (Microsoft)\n- **The Situation:** If you choose to restore from backup, you'll need to get the Oracle DBA involved to validate database consistency after recovery.\n- **Action:** Coordinate with Oracle DBA if opting for backup restore.\n\n---\n\n## ℹ️ FYI (6 items)\n\n**6. ServiceNow Request Canceled - RITM19282296**\n- **From:** IT Service Desk\n- **What happened:** Your ServiceNow Groups and License request was automatically canceled after the approver (Daniel or Cathy) didn't respond to three approval reminders.\n\n**7. Another Cancellation Notice**\n- **From:** IT Service Desk\n- **What happened:** Duplicate notification for the same canceled request (RITM19282296).\n\n**8. Cancellation Comment Added**\n- **From:** IT Service Desk\n- **What happened:** A comment was added to your canceled ServiceNow request (RITM19282296) confirming Daniel and Cathy were notified three times with no action.\n\n**9. February Hardening Scan Reports Available**\n- **From:** Sripriya Vutty (AB InBev)\n- **What happened:** The February hardening scan reports are now published on SharePoint. They're located at the specified path with filename pattern `002_2026_BAU_REPORT_<ZONE>_INT_SCA`.\n- **Action:** Navigate to the SharePoint folder to review if needed.\n\n**10. Another ServiceNow Request Canceled - RITM19282299**\n- **From:** IT Service Desk\n- **What happened:** Another ServiceNow Groups and License request was canceled due to lack of approver response.\n\n**11. Cancellation Comment Added**\n- **From:** IT Service Desk\n- **What happened:** Comment added to the second canceled request (RITM19282299) - same issue, Daniel and Cathy didn't approve despite three notifications.\n\n---\n\n## ❓ Question (1 item)\n\n**12. NAT VM Patching Concerns**\n- **From:** Daniel Gujjarlapudi (AB InBev Security)\n- **What happened:** Daniel is proactively asking if you have any concerns before they proceed with the MGMTNATPAKRP NAT VM patching.\n- **Action:** Let them know if you have any issues.\n\n---\n\n## 🌌 Quick Summary\n\n**Priority Focus Areas:**\n1. **Azure VM boot error** - Decide recovery path and communicate with Microsoft support\n2. **NAT VM patching** - Confirm no concerns or flag issues now\n3. **ServiceNow approvals** - Two requests were auto-canceled - might need to resubmit or follow up with approvers\n\n**Good News:** February hardening scan reports are ready if you need them.\n\nLet me know if you need help drafting responses or want me to follow up on any of these! 🚀"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":1963,"output":1352,"cacheRead":10265,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13580,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1771714826304}}
